{"text": "Fron:\n\nsubjects\n\nPHILIP MORRIS U. S. A. so.\nINTER-OFFICE \u201cCORRESPONDENCE\nRICHMOND, VIRGINIA\nCONFIDENTIAL\nDr. R. B. Seligman pater November 12, 1976\nJ. E, Wickham\n\nGas Phase Analyses\n\nThe data from the recent Readers' Digest article on\nublished in October, 1976 and the data on HCN and NO\nto be published in November, 1976 are given in the attached\ntables. Philip Morris data\u2019are included for comparison\npurposes.\n\nPlease note the CO values in the original publication\nwere expressed in milliliters; whereas, in the second\npublication the \"index\" was reported in milligrams of\ncombined gases. Foster D, Snell laboratories had to convert\nthe CO data from milliliters to milligrams by using the puff\ncount which was not published,\n\nFoster D. Snell employed the following methods for\nthese three gases:\n\n(2) CO - gas chromatography\n(2) HCN - colorimetric analysis similar to the\none used at Philip Morris\n\n(3) NO as NOg - colorimetric analysis (Saltzman reaction)\n\nIn comparing these data, one must realize that smoking\nenvironment can influence the data considerably. Expressing\ndata on a per puff basis would make for a better laboratory to\nlaboratory comparison, \u00b0\n\nThe colorimetric procedure for NO (Saltzman reaction)\nis known to be a very variable analysis. For this reason,\nwe used chemillumenescence or infrared spectroscopy in our\nlaboratories.\n\nJEW: gam\nce:\n\nN. Thonson\nS. Osdene\nF. Gannon\nFagan\nCarpenter\nMeyer\n\nE, Resnik 8\nMeDowe11\nS\ng\n\nAttachments", "words": [{"text": "Fron:", "x0": 69, "y0": 193, "x1": 91, "y1": 201, "conf": 36.0}, {"text": "subjects", "x0": 69, "y0": 219, "x1": 112, "y1": 229, "conf": 73.0}, {"text": "PHILIP", "x0": 302, "y0": 68, "x1": 350, "y1": 80, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "MORRIS", "x0": 360, "y0": 69, "x1": 409, "y1": 81, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "U.", "x0": 418, "y0": 70, "x1": 432, "y1": 81, "conf": 82.0}, {"text": "S.", "x0": 443, "y0": 69, "x1": 457, "y1": 81, "conf": 8